node_modules/
dist/
*.zip
.promptnexus/

# Literature corpora. Third-party published papers, read against the project but
# never ported from — their canonical home is arXiv, and PDF/ alone is 906 MB
# against a 6 MB tracked repository. Documentation/LITERATURE_CORPUS.md records
# what was checked and the SHA-256 of each file checked, which is what makes a
# finding re-verifiable; the bytes themselves are not evidence of anything.
PDF/

# Loose archive extractions. `sources/` is the only place source material is tracked,
# because it is the only place hashes are pinned — verify:sources re-checks all 420 files
# against MANIFEST.json on every build, and a copy outside it is verified by nothing.
#
# These two are not hypothetical clutter. Both hold `promptnexus-v5/prompt_lint.py` with
# FIFTEEN gates, missing DUPLICATE_INSTRUCTION; the frozen `sources/v5/prompt_lint.py` came
# from the later files_4 drop and has sixteen. So an extraction that looks current is a
# linter one gate behind the one the differential oracle compares against.
#
# That is the third time a stale duplicate has turned up beside a frozen original here: a
# nine-stage SystemPromptBuilderPipeline.tsx sits in the repo root with a NEWER mtime than
# the frozen eleven-stage one, and Phase 3 opened by building check:stages because of it.
# Ignoring these keeps the trap out of history without deleting anyone's working copy.
#
# Archives keep being extracted into this working directory while work is going on, so
# `git add -A` here is unsafe: six of these appeared BETWEEN a `git status` and the commit
# that followed it, and swept 327 unintended files into a 4-file change. Stage explicit
# paths in this repository, never `-A` or `.`.
#
# `systempromptbuilder/` carries its own `.git/`, so `git add` records it as a gitlink —
# a submodule pointer to a repository that is not registered anywhere. That one does not
# merely bloat history, it produces a tree git cannot check out cleanly.
Nexus-Prompt/
promptnexus-v5/
PromptNexus-6.2/
System-Prompt-Builder-final-*/
promptnexus5/
synth/
system-prompt-builder-diff-fix/
systempromptbuilder/
#
# `promptnexus-ci/` is filesZ.zip despite the name — catalog.js, PromptNexus.jsx,
# test_app_scope.py and two nested tarballs. It is the historical toolkit archive, NOT CI
# configuration for this repository, which still has none. Its PromptNexus.jsx is 178,520
# bytes against the frozen 179,558 from the later files_4 drop: the fifth stale duplicate
# found beside a frozen original here. Note also that `*.zip` above does not cover the
# `.tar.gz` files inside it.
promptnexus-ci/
#
# `promptnexus-v6-benchmark/` is a specification skeleton, NOT the independent v6
# implementation ADR-0007 wants. That ADR says a v6-equivalent "should be preferred over
# the frozen linter" as the oracle, so this directory is exactly what someone would assume
# had arrived — its `src/lint/prompt_lint.py` is titled "14-Gate Static Analysis Engine"
# and is 29 lines that raise NotImplementedError. Zero gates against the frozen v5's
# sixteen. A name broader than its mechanism, in a filename.
#
# Checked so nobody spends an afternoon wiring it into scripts/differential.ts. If a real
# v6 lands later it belongs in sources/ with a manifest entry, not loose here.
promptnexus-v6-benchmark/

# Model weights. 815 MB against a 6 MB tracked repository, and git keeps blobs forever —
# committing this once makes every future clone carry it whether or not a later commit
# removes it. Weights are also not source: nothing here re-derives or verifies them, and
# the repository has no runtime that loads one.
LLM/

# Generated catalog export bundles. 593 files, five serializations of the same 195 records,
# byte-equivalent to core/src/catalog/techniques.json — the only difference across all 195
# is JSON key order inside usage_templates.
#
# This project does track a generated artifact, techniques.json, but only because
# `check:catalog` re-derives it from the frozen catalog plus catalog-additions.json on every
# build and fails on any drift. NOTHING IN THE REPOSITORY GENERATES THIS BUNDLE, so nothing
# could ever check it. A tracked copy that no checker re-derives is a claim with no verifier.
#
# The name bakes in the record count, so the directory is stale the moment the catalog
# reaches 196 — the fourth stale-duplicate-beside-a-tracked-original here, after the
# nine-stage pipeline component and two copies of a fifteen-gate linter.
#
# If a distributable bundle is wanted, the fix is an exporter script wired into `verify`,
# not a directory committed once and diverging quietly thereafter.
final_bundle_*/
